From befebe25b269314112b145673cae59b1a7ca1094 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sungcheol ahn <donaldahn@google.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 01:01:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Remove serviceClassExists logic to address security
 vulnerability

The serviceClassExists check was identified as a security risk because
it uses createPackageContextAsUser with CONTEXT_INCLUDE_CODE and
CONTEXT_IGNORE_SECURITY, followed by getClassLoader(). This allows a
malicious app to achieve arbitrary code execution in the system_server
process by defining a custom AppComponentFactory.

This change removes the serviceClassExists method and the corresponding
metadata check 'android.telecom.CLASS_EXISTENCE_CHECK' in
InCallController. Telecom will now rely on standard binding mechanisms,
which do not execute third-party code during component resolution.

Bug: 501155244
Test: atest InCallControllerTests
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX
Change-Id: Ibf8d04ad24305da192d4e2cf6ad13c9f3f17484c
---
 .../server/telecom/InCallController.java      |  31 ------
 .../telecom/tests/InCallControllerTests.java  | 104 +-----------------
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 130 deletions(-)

